<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pueblo Revolt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1680">1680</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pueblo Revolt was a coordinated uprising of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pueblo-peoples">Pueblo peoples</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> against Spanish rule that began on 10 August 1680. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope">Popé</a>, the rebels killed about 400 colonists and 21 Franciscan friars, besieged Santa Fe and forced the survivors to retreat south to El Paso. The Pueblos remained independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-vargas">Diego de Vargas</a> reconquered the province from 1692.</p></div>
